; DIMALIGNED with the second origin equal to the first (PT26, #713): the
; dimension is not regenerable (PT23, reason "Points coincide."), so the
; command writes the reason and asks the second origin again (PT5, B12).
; Values by hand from PT23 with ISO-25, as in dimaligned/punti-testo-angolo:
; u = (0.6, 0.8), the location 10 along the normal from the first origin.
DIMALIGNED
10,10
10,10
!report
40,50
; cambia con #930
2,16
